{"id": "EUVD-2026-80427", "enisaUuid": "42944c84-3c51-3fa0-bb90-3b81fe00be9b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amdgpu: avoid force-completing uninitialized UVD rings\n\nuvd_v7_0_sw_init() does not initialize the UVD decode ring for an\nSR-IOV VF. However, amdgpu_uvd_resume() unconditionally force-completes\nthe decode ring when restoring its fence sequence.\n\nSkip fence completion when the fence driver is not initialized.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:30:59", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:48:54", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/668cfb8ab3e22c10fe74307aac86b3cf456d6923", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/863f08c485fbb51b6443681893e4044c7cb6cd51", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dc136795f9997adc8d3219f40e8e3afa7df7183f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/967a179463d3227dfaf9200fd654c1f5a26a11e8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6760f5cb12d2366ddd58a2d8637f7583d73f596b"], "aliases": ["GHSA-9r9g-2xp7-pmx6", "CVE-2026-89827"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "00a26220-544f-3139-907b-41077f967e08", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0a33b11d26c6b7e975b54d469a739ffac29f67ab <dc136795f9997adc8d3219f40e8e3afa7df7183f"}, {"id": "1bfb4f7e-ab66-3882-9daf-6c53fe825235", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "1d0020cd-b25c-3f5b-9e9a-0f4c188ebbaf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0a33b11d26c6b7e975b54d469a739ffac29f67ab <6760f5cb12d2366ddd58a2d8637f7583d73f596b"}, {"id": "2dd69fdb-2989-353b-bdb2-8134baad7314", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.5"}, {"id": "310917b4-2231-3f9f-8cbf-b6815a7cc6ad", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}, {"id": "32e66710-d064-3497-a199-d7303521be41", "product": {"name": "L